    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d314">

                <pb facs="0557" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg453"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.51/3698: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Germany (Dodd)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-10-18T19:00:00-05:00">October 18, 1933—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>132. My 123, October 9, 5 p.m. The Department wishes to determine whether formal
                    protest based on Article VII of Treaty of Friendship, Commerce and Consular
                        Rights<anchor n="94" xml:id="d314-f1"/> is warranted by preferential
                    treatment granted Swiss bondholders. Please telegraph fully and give your
                    recommendations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
